en:
@Y/Tempest@ is English for @K/"great storm"@.
Like the name, let's play with the
force to blow our opponents away.

@Y/Vullcan@ is Latin for @K/"volcano"@.
It's a name that hints at terrifying
power hidden within.

@Y/Avalanche@ means a @K/"rush of snow"@ that
swallows and destroys all in a moment.
It evokes devastating attacking power.

@Y/Sting@ is English for @K/"a sharp blow"@.
Let's hit careless opponents with a
nasty blow, just as the name says.

@Y/Monolith@ is English for @K/"solid rock"@.
Like the name, let our unity repel any
attack or hardship.

@Y/Bandits@ is English for @K/"outlaws"@.
We'll seize the throne or be caught and
lose our strength... it's up to us.

@Y/Blitz@ means @K/"to attack suddenly"@.
It gives the impression of swooping on
the goal and snatching victory.

@Y/Schwarz@ is German for @K/"black"@.
Wouldn't it be a perfect name for us,
all wrapped in a black veil?

@Y/Blaze@ is English for @K/"flames"@.
Let's be a fierce club that burns up
everything it touches, like flames.

@Y/Blues@ is English for @K/"blue"@. A
wonderful name that evokes the vast
expanse of the sky and the sea.

@Y/Shadows@ means @K/"shadow"@ in English.
Let's be a club that creeps up on goal
like a shadow, and leaves foes uneasy.

@Y/Flugel@ is German for @K/"wings"@.
As its name says, let's roam the pitch
freely and take the lead in matches.

@Y/Mantis@ is English for a @K/"mantis"@.
With those sharp scythes, let's become
kings of football, not of insects.

@Y/Geist@ is German for @K/"spirit"@.
With a name like this, let's develop a
spirit that never flinches at any foe.

@Y/Topolino@ is Italian for @K/"mouse"@.
Let's win the crowd over with appealing
play, not just looks.

@Y/Ape@ is Italian for @K/"honeybee"@.
It suggests strong attacks in a swarm,
and light, nimble movement.

@Y/Ballena@ is Spanish for @K/"whale"@.
It's the king of the sea, and we'll aim
to be the kings of the land.

@Y/Blau Wiese@ is German: @K/"blue meadow"@.
It feels easy-going, like a land where
blue grass ripples in the wind.

@Y/Cielo@ is Spanish for @K/"sky"@.
A grand name for a club whose dreams go
beyond the earth towards the heavens.

@Y/Colmillo@ is Spanish for @K/"fang"@.
Wouldn't its fierce, aggressive image
suit us perfectly?

@Y/Corriente@ is Spanish for @K/"current"@.
As the name says, let's show graceful
attacks that flow like water.

@Y/Elf Schritt@ is German for
@K/"11 footsteps"@. It gives the image of
all the players charging ahead as one.

@Y/Espada@ is Spanish for @K/"sword"@.
Let's master attacks that slice through
everything that stands in our way.

@Y/Gluck@ is German for @K/"good fortune"@.
A club the goddess of luck loves must
be the closest to winning the title.

@Y/Herencia@ is Spanish for @K/"legacy"@.
Fine veterans are surely a great legacy
for any club.

@Y/Infini@ is French for @K/"infinity"@.
Our future truly holds infinite
possibilities, doesn't it?

@Y/Lampo@ is Italian for @K/"lightning"@.
A flash of light, then the ball is in
the enemy goal... that'd be cool.

@Y/Leone@ is Italian for @K/"lion"@.
This name gives the impression of a
king, the king of the beasts.

@Y/Lynx@ is French for @K/"lynx"@.
Agile and wild, it's an image that
suits us perfectly, doesn't it?

@Y/Megere@ is French for @K/"spitfire"@.
It feels like a free-spirited club that
doesn't fit any mould.

@Y/Mistral@ is a French @K/"gale"@.
Like the name, let's make our club one
with overwhelming destructive power.

@Y/Panthera@ is Latin for @K/"panther"@.
It brings to mind a club roaming the
pitch freely.

@Y/Riccio@ is Italian for @K/"hedgehog"@.
It sounds a little like calcio, the
word for football.

@Y/Rosa@ is Spanish for @K/"rose"@.
For a club with passion as its symbol,
this name would be a good choice.

@Y/Unicorn@ is English for the
@K/"one-horned beast"@. The name gives a
mystical, noble impression.

@Y/Aurora@ is Italian for @K/"dawn"@.
The dawn of a new era in football...
that is the image it gives.

@Y/Avanzare@ is Italian for @K/"to advance"@.
It suggests a club that drives ever
forward, aiming for win after win.

@Y/El Toro@ is Spanish for @K/"the bull"@.
For a fierce, powerful club, this is
just the right name.

@Y/Estella@ is Spanish for @K/"star"@.
Let's aim to be a brilliant club, the
star attraction of football.

@Y/Feliz@ is Spanish for @K/"fortunate"@.
In matches, the club with the goddess
of luck on its side will win, I think.

@Y/Forte@ is Italian for @K/"strong"@.
I hope this club grows strong enough to
boast of being a match for anyone.

@Y/Gabe@ is German for @K/"gift"@.
Let's be a club where talented players
gather to use their gifts to the full.

@Y/Galeos@ is Greek for @K/"shark"@.
It brings to mind sharp shark's teeth,
biting into their half with the ball.

@Y/Giurare@ is Italian for @K/"to swear"@.
With the crowd, let's vow to the god
of football to play superbly and win!

@Y/Iris@ is Greek for @K/"rainbow"@.
A rainbow is the one tie between earth
and sky. Build a bridge to victory.

@Y/Lumiere@ is French for @K/"light"@.
Let's play as fast as light and as
dazzling as light.

@Y/Mythos@ is German for @K/"myth"@.
Let's write a new myth in football and
become a club talked about forever.

@Y/Plaisir@ is French for @K/"pleasure"@.
Let's be a club that enjoys playing
the game together with the crowd.

@Y/Rafale@ is French for @K/"gust"@.
It suggests quick, attacking play, like
a sudden gust of wind.

@Y/Rendir@ is Spanish for @K/"to defeat"@.
It suggests the strongest club of all,
one that forces every rival to submit.

@Y/Salire@ is Italian for @K/"to climb"@.
Like climbers heading for the summit,
let's aim to be the strongest club.

@Y/Sfida@ is Italian for @K/"challenge"@.
Never get complacent. Only a club that
keeps challenging is a true champion.

@Y/Stolz@ is German for @K/"pride"@.
Let's always play in a way that we can
take pride in as professionals.

@Y/Tigre@ is Italian for @K/"tiger"@.
Let's win the crown with powerful,
swift play, like a tiger.

@Y/Valentia@ is Spanish for @K/"courage"@.
I can see us attacking boldly with
courage deep into enemy territory.
